#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:5
#: 47f438a69e18414eaa865e2098eac02e
msgid "Setting Motor Range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:7
#: 9509bba69fd745cc9e619d19ad7d7e33
msgid "Most ESCs have a dead zone at the bottom of their range.  This page outlines how to test the size of the range and then set the spin-when-armed and min throttle values appropriately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:9
#: 043fc5c4f7f74dc1b6dafe4c756356ed
msgid "Although not required, advanced users may wish to take the next step by measuring and adjusting the :ref:`motor thrust curve <motor-thrust-scaling>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:13
#: 38dfaf8f003448fdb01f5b77c862eb8d
msgid "Please complete the :ref:`ESC calibration <esc-calibration>` before setting the motor range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:16
#: a2769518c0c24a1395c27467987107a6
msgid "Measuring the deadzone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:18
#: bfd0a6d2b70946f1aaa2db6f097fabcc
msgid "Remove the propellers from the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:19
#: f501bb95422d40eca39ab70060fa6575
msgid "Connect the LiPo battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:20
#: 9ea8d7866ad246a59f2d053a40b89d49
msgid "Connect the autopilot to the Mission Planner using a USB cable or telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:21
#: 0345923c87a4420685630f598aec70e8
msgid "Open the Mission Planner's Initial Setup >> Optional Hardware >> Motor Test page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:26
#: 11088fc0f35c458f8a351f71bfccf2ce
msgid "Increase the \"Throttle %\" field and push each of the \"Test motor\" buttons to determine what percentage is required for each of the motors to spin.  If all ESCs are from the same manufacturer they will likely all have similar dead zones, but having one or two different by 1% ~ 2% is common.  Pick the highest percentage of all the motors - we will use this below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:29
#: 7d0887448dc144e3842aef4b9ec0d55d
msgid "Setting Spin-Armed and Min Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:31
#: 8026ee668cd84eebafbf9d057dc1b002
msgid "By default, when the vehicle is armed but not flying, the motors will spin at a slightly slower than normal speed.  This speed can be configured using :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` parameter. Once the vehicle is flying, we want to ensure that we never output a value that causes the motors to stop spinning, this lower limit can be configured :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN<MOT_SPIN_MIN>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:34
#: ed9d52e60524414fbe307ca4f972f404
msgid "set the :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` parameter to **(the percentage discovered above + 2%) / 100**.  I.e. if you found the deadzone of the ESCs was 7%, set :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` to 0.09 (i.e (7 + 2) / 100)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:35
#: 4319c62b29714fd0a6a9ca969eca3e98
msgid "set the :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` parameter to at least 0.03 higher than :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>`.  I.e. if :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` was 0.09, set :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` to 0.12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:39
#: 98ceb497257a42dcb07a5cecfc663a4c
msgid "Setting :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` even higher than recommended above is acceptable if we want to account for voltage drop of the battery, but setting it too high reduces the lower range of the motors which reduces control which could be important, especially on powerful copters with a low hover throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:43
#: 68b5ae2865e54aaa890712a1bf2d2d80
msgid "The :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MAX <MOT_SPIN_MAX>` parameter to account for the very top of the ESC/motor range which generally produces no additional thrust.  By default this value is 0.95 (i.e. top 5% of the range produces no additional thrust)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:45
#: f7a9f5663ff64df19179ebfe8c5f1527
msgid "if ESC RPM telemetry is being used, the :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MIN<TKOFF_RPM_MIN>` parameter could be set slightly below the :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` parameter to prevent takeoff attempts, and subsequent flips on takeoff, if one or more motors are not spinning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:48
#: 1065cb92de9b40398810c8a14a2f3369
msgid "IDLE State Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/set-motor-range.rst:49
#: c8fb1d8461cd4a7997f45680ef0151c8
msgid "If needed, you can add delay between the time the motor idle state is reached and when increased throttle can be applied to the ESCs using the :ref:`MOT_IDLE_SEC <MOT_IDLE_SEC>` parameter (default is 0 seconds)."
msgstr ""
